    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0346" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg266"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1072.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    translation of a proclamation of his excellency Viceroy Yuan Shih-k’ai,
                    published in the Chihli Gazette of the 19th instant, concerning the “Boxer
                    heresy.”</p>
                <p>I have no doubt the viceroy is in earnest. If he shall be properly supported by
                    the Throne there will be little further trouble with Boxers in this
                    province.</p>
                <p>We can not, however, forget that in 1900 Yuan Shih-k’ai started out in the same
                    way, as governor of Shantung, but instead of being sustained by the Court he was
                    instructed not to use such severe measures. I think we may hope for better
                    things now.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d215-a1.xml" xpointer="d215-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
